Package: mica-wifi
Version: 2.12-mica1
Source-Date-Epoch: 1790380800
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Mica OS <hi@micaos.dev>
Section: net
Priority: optional
Depends: libc6, libnl-3-200, libnl-genl-3-200, libssl3t64, iw, rfkill
Description: Mica OS Wi-Fi station: a minimal wpa_supplicant
 /usr/sbin/wpa_supplicant and /usr/sbin/wpa_cli compiled from the upstream
 hostap release with the nl80211 driver only, and WPA2 and WPA3 personal
 through the root's OpenSSL. No D-Bus interface, smartcard, WPS, P2P, mesh or
 enterprise EAP.
 .
 wpa_supplicant@.service is installed and not enabled: micad starts one
 instance per interface and renders its
 /etc/wpa_supplicant/wpa_supplicant-<interface>.conf. /etc is inside the
 read-only root, so etc-wpa_supplicant.mount binds /etc/wpa_supplicant from
 the STATE partition, where the PSKs also survive an A/B update.
 mica-regdb-reload.service loads the wireless regulatory database before a
 radio is configured.
 .
 Access-point support is mica-wifi-ap.
